      "body": "## Overview\n\nAdd `tests/utils_/test_math_utils.py` covering `prev_power_of_2`, `largest_power_of_2_divisor`, and `round_up_to`, which previously had no tests anywhere in `tests/`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- 32 boundary cases for three bit-twiddling helpers whose off-by-one errors propagate into block-size and alignment math.\n- CPU-only, no GPU, no downloads.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `pytest tests/utils_/test_math_utils.py -v` locally: 32 passed.\n- `ruff check` and `ruff format --check` clean.\n- Also verified via the standard path (real `vllm` import chain and repo conftest, no stubbing, no `--noconftest`): 32 passed.\n\n## Details\n\n- Cases cover exact powers, values between powers, non-positive inputs, exact matches, gaps, and the above-all-values `None` case for `round_up_to`.\n\nAI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\nThis PR is not duplicating an existing PR: open PRs were searched for the covered area keywords on Oct 30, 2026, with no matches.",
